From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-mini4: Give the display pipe its eDP
 link

The iPad mini 4's panel is eDP, not MIPI DSI. Its Apple device trees
(iOS 12.4, 16G77, j96ap and j97ap; the two agree on everything here)
have no mipi-dsim node but a displayport node: "displayport,t7000",
embedded, four lanes, its registers at 0x206700000 (0x1000), power and
clock gate 114 (ps_dp), an "lpdp-phy,t7000" PHY and an "lcd,edp" panel.
disp0 and dart-disp0 are otherwise the iPod touch 6's: the same windows,
interrupts (103, 108-111 and 106, 107), gates, error reflector,
fetch and diag configuration.

Give the pipe the dp power domain in place of t7000.dtsi's mipi_dsi, as
the boot framebuffer already has, and the transmitter's window as "dp",
as the iPad 5's pipe has it. The driver then names the connector eDP.

The panel supply is left out. The ADT's function-lcd_ldo is PMU GPIO 17
(read), but the driver switches it off in system sleep and retrains the
link over the transmitter's AUX channel on wake, with register offsets
taken from the A9's transmitter. The mini 4's kernelcache drives both
SoCs' transmitters from the same AppleANXDPTX kext, but through separate
AppleT7000DPTXController and AppleS8000DPTXController classes, and the
offsets have not been compared. Until they are, the panel stays on in
system sleep, as under simpledrm, and the driver never touches the
transmitter.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
index 08d3b41..d067921 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-mini4.dtsi
@@ -171,6 +171,20 @@
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0 &ps_dp>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * ADT displayport ("displayport,t7000", embedded, four lanes): the panel
+ * link is eDP, so the pipe holds the dp domain instead of mipi_dsi and
+ * gets the transmitter's window.
+ */
+&disp0 {
+	reg = <0x2 0x06200000 0x0 0x100000>,
+	      <0x2 0x06304000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x2 0x06300000 0x0 0x4000>,
+	      <0x2 0x06700000 0x0 0x1000>;
+	reg-names = "adp", "dart0", "dart1", "dp";
+	power-domains = <&ps_disp0>, <&ps_dp>;
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
